# counter/_websocket scope 300 — answer on the same socket.
#
# `reply` targets the session this envelope came from; `text` given as an
# object is sent as JSON text, so the browser receives {"count": N}.
# (`txco://websocket/send WITH session_id = @websocket.session.id` is the
# explicit spelling, and the one to use from any other run — a cron, an
# HTTP request — that wants to push to a known session.)
WHEN .msg.type == "increment"
  EXEC "txco://websocket/reply"
  WITH text.count = ._kv
